# SAMA Knowledge Base v2 — IDE session memory

IDE/agent continuity only. For facts, prefer live project docs over memory.

## Read first (in order)

1. `README.md` — layout, stages, what changed from v1 and why
2. `docs/PIPELINE.md` — data flow, artifacts, cost control
3. `docs/SESSION.md` — runbook and open items
4. `docs/agents/README.md` — Orchestrator → Legal → Mapper → Extractor → Reviewer → Formatter

## Source-of-truth hierarchy

| Topic | Authoritative location |
|---|---|
| Layout & commands | `README.md` |
| Data flow & artifacts | `docs/PIPELINE.md` |
| Paths, thresholds, models | `sama/config.py` |
| Session state / todos | `docs/SESSION.md` |
| Agent personas | `docs/agents/` |
| Regulatory text | `corpus/markdown/*.md` |
| Graph navigation | `SAMA_Knowledge_Base_Obsidian/_INDEX_Routing.md` |
| Conversion QA | `reports/conversion/` |
| Graph QA | `reports/graph/` |

**Corpus text wins** over graph enrichment or Obsidian paraphrase when quoting law.

## How this repo is used

- One entry point: `python run.py --all` (stages: crawl → convert → build → enrich → audit).
- `python run.py --all --dry-run` reports what is wired up without spending anything.
- Graphify ingest root is `corpus/` (markdown only).
- Enrichment has a free tier (grounding, locators, caveats, routing index) and a
  paid tier (node summaries, community themes, ~22% of edge narratives).
  `--skip-model` runs the free tier alone.
- This is a **first-run** pipeline: there is no baseline, delta or update mode.

## Do not

- Hardcode paths, thresholds or model names anywhere but `sama/config.py`.
- Hardcode node/edge counts — read `graphify-out/graph.json` or the audit report.
- Put secrets in docs, rules or committed files.
- Re-run a full extract or a paid enrichment pass unless the user asks.
- Reintroduce `arabic-reshaper` / `python-bidi`: they emit display-order
  presentation forms, which is the defect v2 exists to fix.
- Rewrite agent personas in-chat as a parallel source; edit `docs/agents/`.
